1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:07,433
IFC ClashTrace. Geometry. Result. Evidence. Every relationship, traceable.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:17,100
When a pipe meets structure, a reviewer needs more than a coloured marker. They need to know what was tested, which rule fired, and why.

3
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:30,200
Start with two IFC4 files. They stay in the browser. Before the run, the interface keeps file roles, supported boundaries, and evidence expectations in view.

4
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,433
Choose the MEP IFC.

5
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,867
Choose the structural IFC.

6
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,100
Confirm shared coordinates.

7
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,267
Then run one deterministic review.

8
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:58,067
This controlled example is a synthetic twelve-by-eight-metre clinic: seven represented pipe routes, plus one pipe segment with no geometry.

9
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:09,400
Eighty-eight wall-and-beam relationships resolve to four clashes, one clearance warning, eleven not-evaluated records, and seventy-two passes.

10
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:22,333
Select a record. The three-dimensional view isolates the pipe and structure, while the evidence panel shows component types, rule, measurement, and evaluation boundary.

11
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:35,833
The boundary is explicit. Interior depth must be greater than two millimetres for a hard clash. Forty-nine millimetres triggers a clearance warning. Fifty millimetres does not.

12
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:48,233
If geometry, coordinates, units, or reliability fall outside the supported contract, the result is not evaluated—not quietly passed.

13
00:01:50,133 --> 00:02:03,300
Controlled tests keep that logic honest: eight of eight authored cases agree with an independent reference and the browser core; nine of nine clearance fixtures agree across both evaluator routes.

14
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:17,233
AI remains separate. A four-record review pack exposes only minimal derived fields, requires fresh consent, and cannot change deterministic status or measurement.

15
00:02:20,133 --> 00:02:31,700
This is a focused feasibility prototype for IFC4 STEP, unprefixed metre units, established shared coordinates, and pipe relationships against walls and beams.

16
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:46,233
It is not engineering certification, and it does not claim accuracy for arbitrary projects. It offers a disciplined review path: geometry, result, evidence. Every relationship, traceable.
